---
// /docs — the docs overview: how Agentry fits together. Facts match the landing page.
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs-layout/DocsLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../lib/base.ts";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="How Agentry fits together"
  description="How Agentry fits together: one front door that sizes the process to the task, specialist agents, your board as verified lanes, a local memory and one CLI."
  eyebrow="Docs · Overview"
  lede="Agentry is an adaptive agentic layer for Claude Code, with OpenCode support in development. It routes a task to the least process that wins, conducts the work with SDLC specialists, and gates the result with you — so the bar is held instead of hoped for."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Every task enters through one front door — <code>/agentry:go</code> — and gets routed to the
      <em>least process that wins</em>: a clear, reversible change runs <strong>one-shot</strong>;
      an under-specified goal is shaped <strong>spec-first</strong> before any code; a multi-file,
      structurally non-trivial change is run <strong>decompose+verify</strong> — sliced into bounded
      tasks, built by specialists, and checked by an independent verifier. Agentry conducts that work
      with SDLC specialists (product, architect, implementer, verifier, librarian) and gates the
      result with you at the decision points that matter.
    </p>

    <h2 class="prose__h">What's in the box</h2>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><strong>9 agents</strong>, each with one job, called only when the work earns them.</li>
      <li><strong>15 skills</strong> that carry the craft the agents load: architecting, planning, implementing, testing, reviewing, designing and more.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your board, as lanes.</strong> <code>/agentry:exec</code> runs a task whose contract is
        already written in its own worktree, with a builder, an independent verifier and your gate;
        <code>/agentry:merge</code> lands it. <strong>17 board rules</strong> mirror the checks you
        already run. See <a href={withBase("docs/lanes/")}>Lanes</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A local memory, <code>agentry mem</code>.</strong> Decisions, gotchas and repo facts as
        plain files, recalled when a task needs them. See <a href={withBase("docs/memory/")}>Memory</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>One CLI, <code>agentry</code>.</strong> Every move the slash commands make is a command
        you can script.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="prose__cta">
      New here? Start with the <a href={withBase("docs/quickstart/")}>Quickstart</a>, or
      <a href={withBase("") + "#install"}>install Agentry</a> and run your first task through
      <code>/agentry:go</code>.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
